Volunteer Program at PE Insights

Nordic's Largest PE Conference. Stockholm, November 24th &amp; 25th 2027

&nbsp;

Ready to take a major leap towards private equity, M&amp;A, banking or consulting? This is your chance to get a view behind the scenes of the world’s largest private equity community and be part of the volunteer team shaping the future of finance.

Challenge yourself to go outside your comfort zone with likeminded individuals who for two days will be your partners in the trenches facilitating the room of top-of-the pyramid PE professionals.

&nbsp;

Why Private Equity Insights

Private Equity Insights is the world’s largest Private Equity community with 1m PE professionals, delivering impact through 12 global PE conferences with thousands of the most world’s best investors and operators such as Blackstone, BlackRock, Apollo, Carlyle, CVC, KKR, and many more.&nbsp;

Private Equity Insights is part of United Media (https://www.united-media.com/) which focuses on building large-scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, finance, retail, etc. As of today, we have organically launched 5 media companies and exited 1.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What we offer you

You’ll be supporting the Private Equity Insights team in delivering the conference for sharp insights and inspiration, and outstanding network opportunities for the PE professionals we serve. Among other things the opportunity offer:

• Peer network: you join a select group of ambitious volunteers who will keep crossing your path for the next 40 years working in the industry.

• Insider knowledge. Where the day allows, you can sit in on panels, the same ones attendees come to hear. In fact, we encourage you to do so.

• Confidence under pressure: after two demanding conference days, high-stakes moments at work will feel easier.

• Master persuasion: learn to influence high-caliber professionals to deliver win-win results.&nbsp;

• A certificate to show on your CV and LinkedIn that you volunteered at Private Equity Insights.&nbsp;

• Fuel: food and refreshments on both days.

• Global programme: The long term opportunity to lead teams and become the person who shows the way for others, or even join Private Equity Insights full time.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Your responsibilities

This is hands-on, operational work focusing on making the conference run. The work changes hour by hour, and you are expected to step in and help wherever the conference needs you.

&nbsp;

What the future hold for you with PE Insights&nbsp;

Whether you are with us for 1 conference or 10+, we believe this lays the foundation for a very successful career.&nbsp;

Exceptional volunteers have in the past been offered roles at Private Equity Insights, such as Investor Relations or Entrepreneur in Residence.

Others have gone on to join firms such as McKinsey, BCG, JP Morgan, Deutsche Bank, Ardian and Verdane.

&nbsp;

What we expect from you

We are looking for final-year undergraduates, master's students and early-career professionals with an interest in private equity, M&amp;A, banking, consulting or conferences. We expect you to:

• Have a relentless drive to become the very best at what you do

• Bring outstanding energy and a positive mindset from the first hour to the last

• Set aside 2 full days for the conference + online training leading up to

• Be curious to learn from top private equity professionals

• Stand out as the person others want beside them on a hard day

• Speak English at a professional level. Spanish is a plus

&nbsp;

This is an unpaid role. Applicants from outside Stockholm are welcome. You fully arrange your own travel and accommodation.&nbsp;

We review every application and invite shortlisted candidates to a short call. If you hold yourself to the standard described here, apply.

About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Role Summary and Impact

As a Senior Associate, Performance, you will be a vital engine driving client success by supporting your team with the execution and optimization of performance media campaigns across search, social, and display channels. You will directly impact client revenue growth by strategically managing campaigns and identifying opportunities for improved performance. Your work will have a significant impact on the overall success of our clients' marketing efforts, contributing to increased brand awareness and customer acquisition.&nbsp;

• Proactively contributing&nbsp;to achieving client performance goals by implementing effective campaign strategies and optimization techniques.&nbsp;

• Executing&nbsp;thorough Search Query Report (SQR) analysis to identify irrelevant or low-performing keywords, implementing negative keywords, and optimizing keyword bidding strategies for improved campaign efficiency.&nbsp;

• Developing&nbsp;and&nbsp;presenting&nbsp;comprehensive weekly performance reports, analyzing key metrics and translating data into clear, actionable recommendations for campaign improvement.&nbsp;

• Overseeing&nbsp;the analysis of campaign results, identifying trends, drawing conclusions, and documenting key learnings to inform future campaign strategies and best practices.&nbsp;

• Analyzing&nbsp;user engagement metrics (e.g., click-through rates, conversion rates, bounce rates) to identify opportunities for optimizing ad creative, landing pages, and targeting parameters to improve overall campaign performance.&nbsp;

• Conducting&nbsp;in-depth reporting and analysis of paid media performance and audience behavior, identifying key trends and insights to inform strategic decisions related to targeting, messaging, and budget allocation.&nbsp;

• Overseeing&nbsp;finance reconciliation processes, verifying campaign spend, identifying discrepancies, and ensuring accurate financial reporting and budget management.&nbsp;

Skills and Experience

• Minimum of 2 years of experience in digital media, paid advertising, or media buying (agency experience a plus!).&nbsp;

• A proven track record of managing successful paid search and social campaigns.&nbsp;

• Exceptional analytical skills and the ability to translate data into actionable insights.&nbsp;

• A creative and solutions-oriented mindset.&nbsp;

• Excellent communication and collaboration skills.&nbsp;

• A meticulous and organized approach to work.&nbsp;

Life at WPP Media &amp; Benefits

Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we’re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

